+/**
+ * Process-wide singleton "owner" wrapper around pimMSILoop, the install step
+ * that drives Windows Installer (msiexec/MSI API) package installs. One of
+ * 7 near-identical Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core.
+ *
+ * Locking contract DIVERGES from its 5 TryLock-based siblings
+ * (pimCopier/pimShortcuts/pimRegEdit/pimServices/pimDownloader): this class
+ * has no internal xmlMutex at all. Instead it gates entry via the external
+ * pimOKToRunMsiexec()/pimFreeMsiexec() functions (pim_util), which this
+ * class SHARES with pimSFXCopier -- confirmed: both classes call the exact
+ * same functions. Consequence: at most one of {an MSI install via this
+ * class, an SFX install via pimSFXCopier} can be in flight process-wide at
+ * any moment. pimOKToRunMsiexec() additionally probes the Windows Installer
+ * "...\\Installer\\InProgress" registry key, so this gate can also fail
+ * closed due to an MSI operation running OUTSIDE this process entirely.
+ *
+ * Unlike its siblings, Status()'s "done" branch does NOT delete the owned
+ * pimMSILoop or release the gate -- cleanup is caller-driven via Release()/
+ * Kill(). A caller that never calls Release() after a normal completion
+ * leaves the shared MSI/SFX gate held indefinitely.
+ *
+ * Sole caller in this codebase: pimEntitlement.
+ */
 class pimMSICopier
 {
 private:
